          "filename": "Tadjoura sultan Mohammed Leitah 1885-1889.jpg",
          "caption": "Engraving based on a photograph showing Sultan Hummad bin Muhammad (Mohammed \"Leitah\") of Tadjoura, now in Djibouti, with Afar chiefs c. 1885-1889. The engraving accompanied an article in the 21 April 1889 issue of Le Journal des Voyages about the attempt by Russian Cossack Nikolay Ivanovitch Achinov to establish a Russian settlement at Sagalo, near Tadjoura, at the end of 1888. The Sultan had allegedly granted him land for the project.",
